    "Koalas have fingerprints that are nearly indistinguishable from human ones.",
    "Dolphins give each other individual names in the form of signature whistles.",
    "Pistol shrimp snap a claw so fast that the shockwave stuns their prey.",
    "Bombardier beetles can spray a boiling chemical mixture to defend themselves.",
    "Some turtles can breathe through their cloaca.",
    "A group of flamingos is called a flamboyance.",
    "A group of crows is called a murder.",
    "Sharks existed before trees did.",
    "Elephants are among the few animals that cannot jump.",
    "Mantis shrimp have up to sixteen types of colour receptor, while humans have three.",
