    "Potatoes were first domesticated thousands of years ago in the Andes.",
    "The Margherita pizza is said to be named after Queen Margherita of Italy, who visited Naples in 1889.",

    # History and culture
    "Oxford University was teaching students before the Aztec city of Tenochtitlan was founded.",
    "Cleopatra lived closer in time to the Moon landing than to the building of the Great Pyramid.",
    "Woolly mammoths were still alive on Wrangel Island when the Great Pyramid was built.",
    "The Anglo-Zanzibar War of 1896 is the shortest war on record, lasting about 38 to 45 minutes.",
    "Napoleon was of average height for his time; the myth of his shortness came partly from British propaganda.",
    "Vikings did not wear horned helmets; no archaeological evidence for them has been found.",
    "The Scottish national animal is the unicorn.",
    "The Great Wall of China is generally not visible to the naked eye from low Earth orbit.",
    "The Post-it note was invented by accident, when a 3M chemist made a weak adhesive.",
    "The Wright brothers' first powered flight in 1903 lasted 12 seconds and covered 120 feet.",
    "Basketball was invented in 1891 using peach baskets as the goals.",
    "The first YouTube video, 'Me at the zoo', was uploaded in 2005.",
    "The first computer bug was a real moth, found stuck in a relay in 1947.",

    # Japan
    "Japan has more than 6,800 islands.",
    "Japan has around four million vending machines.",
    "No passenger on a Shinkansen bullet train has died in a derailment or collision since the line opened in 1964.",
    "The Japanese word 'tsundoku' describes buying books and leaving them unread.",
    "The English word 'tsunami' comes from Japanese, meaning 'harbour wave'.",

    # Language and numbers
    "The verb 'run' has more senses in the Oxford English Dictionary than almost any other English word.",
    "A googol is 1 followed by 100 zeros.",
    "Pi has been calculated to more than 100 trillion digits.",
    "There are exactly five Platonic solids.",
    "The Rubik's Cube has 43 quintillion possible arrangements.",
    "Zero was used as a placeholder for centuries before it was treated as a number in its own right.",

    # Technology
